From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: add a tuning file for the OV5648

The software ISP has no per-sensor tuning at all, so every OV5648 falls back
to uncalibrated.yaml, which leaves the black level to be guessed from the
luminance histogram (redone whenever exposure or gain changes, so the black
point follows the scene rather than the sensor).

Pin the black level, and add a colour correction matrix. On the PineTab 2 the
software-ISP debayer delivers green and blue swapped for this sensor's GBRG
binned modes, so the CCM swaps them back (rows 2 and 3) and applies a
saturation boost; rows sum to 1 so neutrals stay neutral. The matrix was
hand-tuned on a PineTab 2 - a chart-measured CCM would be the clean upstream
form, but this gives correct hues instead of a green/blue swap.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN tu_a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build tu_b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-09-18 19:06:58.756687466 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-09-18 19:06:58.778036754 +0200
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0

 conf_files = files([
+    'ov5648.yaml',
     'uncalibrated.yaml',
 ])

diff -ruN tu_a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml tu_b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml	2026-09-18 19:06:58.765052712 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+%YAML 1.1
+---
+version: 1
+algorithms:
+  - BlackLevel:
+      # Measured on a PineTab 2: with the sensor covered the raw 10-bit
+      # readout floors at 16, so the pedestal is 16/1023 -> 1024 in the
+      # 16-bit units this file uses.
+      blackLevel: 1024
+  - Awb:
+  - Ccm:
+      # The soft-ISP debayer delivers green and blue swapped for this sensor's
+      # GBRG binned modes, so the matrix swaps them back (rows 2 and 3) and
+      # adds a saturation boost. Rows sum to 1 so neutrals stay neutral.
+      ccms:
+        - ct: 6500
+          ccm: [  2.10, -0.55, -0.55,
+                 -0.55, -0.55,  2.10,
+                 -0.55,  2.10, -0.55 ]
+  - Adjust:
+  - Agc:
+...
